\f0\b \cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 The .phone shell, and scroll lock behind the open sheet
\f1\b0 \cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0Code dependency, outside this screen. Two parts. First, .phone-body must stop being the scroll container: while it keeps overflow-y: auto the seventeen form frames have no viewport to stick their footers to, and the same change adds the bottom safe-area inset. Second, Today must not scroll behind the open sheet \'97 a scroll lock on the layer beneath, released on close, with the list's position preserved so dismissing the sheet returns the athlete to where they tapped. Test on iPhone Safari: it is the case where a locked underlayer most often leaks the scroll or jumps to the top on release. Both parts affect all four athlete entry forms at once.\'a0
